  "id": "COMPOUND:30686 - PROTEIN:4886",
  "verbalization": "Capsianoside L is implicated in the regulation of Serine/threonine-protein kinase ATR through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Capsianoside L acts as a target for Peripheral myelin protein 22, which in turn is targeted by two different compounds: 2-(2-((2E)-3,7-Dimethyl-2,6-octadien-1-yl)-5-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenyl)-6-benzofuranol and Chaetomugilin I. Both of these compounds are linked to the activation of ATR, a serine/threonine-protein kinase. The presence of multiple pathways converging on ATR indicates a potential role for Capsianoside L in modulating ATR activity through its interaction with these targets. The consistent scores across the paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction between Capsianoside L and ATR remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the signaling network and underscores the importance of further investigation into the molecular mechanisms underlying this relationship.",
